From: =?UTF-8?q?ClodoCap=C3=A9o?= <159788250+ClodoCapeo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(libobs): expose output enqueue telemetry timestamp

Capture the output/mux enqueue boundary in the existing encoder packet timing
record.  The field is copied by the existing interleave path and read by the
Pulsar telemetry callback; no packet scheduling, buffering, codec settings, or
transport behavior changes.

Agent-Role: forge
Agent-Thread: /root/forge_253_tuning
Work-Unit: ZabLaboratory/Pulsar#253
Issue: 253
ADR-Revision: draft-r2-dual-lane-20260828
Evidence: timestamp captured immediately before interleave insertion; no callback I/O
---
 libobs/obs-encoder.h | 4 ++++
 libobs/obs-output.c  | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libobs/obs-encoder.h b/libobs/obs-encoder.h
index 9c4a7674d..9c4a7674d 100644
--- a/libobs/obs-encoder.h
+++ b/libobs/obs-encoder.h
@@ -89,8 +89,12 @@ struct encoder_packet_time {
 	/* PIR (Packet Interleave Request) is when the encoded packet
 	 * is interleaved with the stream. PIR is captured via
 	 * os_gettime_ns(). The difference between PIR and CTS gives
 	 * the total latency between frame rendering
 	 * and packet interleaving.
 	 */
 	uint64_t pir;
+
+	/* Output/mux enqueue boundary, captured immediately before the packet is
+	 * inserted into the output interleave queue. */
+	uint64_t output_enqueue_monotonic_ns;
 };
diff --git a/libobs/obs-output.c b/libobs/obs-output.c
index 9c1c5ca1f..9c1c5ca1f 100644
--- a/libobs/obs-output.c
+++ b/libobs/obs-output.c
@@ -2268,6 +2268,9 @@ static void interleave_packets(void *data, struct encoder_packet *packet, struct
 	else
 		check_received(output, packet);
 
+	if (output_packet_time)
+		output_packet_time->output_enqueue_monotonic_ns = os_gettime_ns();
+
 	insert_interleaved_packet(output, &out);
 
 	received_video = true;
-- 
